                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 28,
                "retweet_count": 27,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Today is Medicaid Matters Day of Action, and I\u2019m speaking out because nearly 15 million Californians rely on Medicaid\u2014known in our state as Medi-Cal\u2014for their health care. That\u2019s more than one in three Californians who depend on this program to see a doctor, afford prescriptions and get the care they need.\n\nRepublicans in Congress have proposed slashing $880 billion from Medicaid. Let\u2019s be clear: that would devastate families in Sacramento County and across America. These aren\u2019t just numbers\u2014they\u2019re real people, real families and real lives at risk.\n\nAs a doctor, I\u2019ve seen firsthand what happens when patients can\u2019t afford care. As a member of the Congressional Doctors Caucus, I\u2019m bringing that experience to Congress and pushing back against these dangerous cuts. I\u2019ll keep fighting to protect Medicaid and make sure every American gets the care they deserve.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1744921802,
                "view_count": 6562
